      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For hidden losses like counting errors or damages, you should incorporate a \"shrinkage factor\" alongside the variability calculations. You can estimate the average loss percentage and use this to inflate your safety stock recommendation, essentially treating it as a systematic demand or supply uncertainty. Alternatively, adjust your expected lead time or inbound quantity based on historical loss rates to create a more conservative buffer in your safety stock calculation.",
